PRE-TABLE CHECK -- #521 mk48nvramkill
Written BEFORE table 1 runs, so this file's own mtime proves the order.

THE DIFF UNDER TEST is ONE token: the accept block's lower bound goes from
`relative_addr < MK48T08_CLKOFF' to `relative_addr < MK48T08_CLKOFF + MK48TXX_ICSR'.
Everything else in the hunk is comment.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- SIBLING PARITY

The two bounds of the accept block are the siblings, and they are ASYMMETRIC ON PURPOSE:

    lower  CLKOFF + ICSR   (0x1ff8)   -- CHANGED by this diff
    upper  CLKOFF + ISEC   (0x1ff9)   -- UNCHANGED

After the change the block admits everything except the single offset 0x1ff8, which is
exactly the one case the switch implements.  The asymmetry is therefore not an oversight:
the window has collapsed to the width of the implemented case.

  ROW OWED, and it is the one this check exists to find: the upper bound is now load-
  bearing in a way it was not before.  Before the diff, moving it would have shifted a
  nine-offset window; after it, moving it by one either swallows the implemented case
  (ISEC -> ICSR, window empty) or re-admits a clock register (ISEC -> ISEC+1).  Rows
  `ok rd 1ff8' / `ok wr 1ff8' and `ok rd 1ff9' / `ok wr 1ff9' already exist and pin both
  sides.  NO NEW ROW OWED -- discharged by rows the witness already carried.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- CLAIM -> ROW

Added comment sentences asserting an observable consequence:

  "the eight offsets 0x1ff0..0x1ff7 fell through it to a `default:' that calls exit(1)"
      -> ROWED, sixteen times: `rd 1ff0'..`rd 1ff7', `wr 1ff0'..`wr 1ff7', each paired
         with its ` obs' row.
  "every offset kills in BOTH directions"
      -> ROWED by construction: the census IS both directions.
  "the kill is WIDTH-INDEPENDENT ... there is no width axis here"
      -> *** NO ROW, AND THE NO-ROW IS THE POINT. ***  `len' never enters the guard, so a
         row varying width at a fixed offset CANNOT VARY under any mutant of this guard.
         It would be vacuous by construction -- the CHANNEL failure this project names.
         The claim is a statement about the ABSENCE of an axis and is discharged by the
         enumeration in the comment, not by a row.  Measured by the witness at three
         widths (ld, ld.h, ld.bu) all dying at the same start offset.
  "storage already existed -- `reg' is MK48TXX_LEN bytes"
      -> ROWED indirectly by every ` obs' row and directly by `live' (a byte round-trips
         through the same decode) and `nvram0' (an unwritten neighbour reads 0).
  "the upper bound stays at MK48TXX_ISEC deliberately"
      -> ROWED by `ok rd/wr 1ff9'.

--------------------------------------------------------- GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD

  guard reads:  relative_addr            (and the two vendored constants)
  body reads:   relative_addr, idata, writeflag, d->reg[]

`relative_addr' is the ONLY field in both.  There is no second field whose disagreement
with the guard's could hide a state -- which is why this round has no joint-cell
obligation, unlike the recent PCC2 and MTE rounds.  `idata' and `writeflag' are inputs the
guard does not test; `writeflag' IS partitioned by the body (`if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)'),
so the {offset} x {read, write} cross-product is a floor axis and IS FULLY ROWED -- sixteen
cells, all sixteen driven.

  DISCLOSED, clause (e): `idata' is not partitioned by the body -- it is stored whole -- so
  its value space is a single cell and no row is owed per value.  The witness drives 0x5a.

