PASS 2 FOUND TWO MORE THINGS AND ONE OF THEM WAS AN APPARATUS DEFECT IN THIS VERY TABLE.
Table 3 (t3/SCORES.txt) is the result.  ZERO ESCAPES.

  BASE      57/57
  M_OLD     16/57      M_HALF  36/57      M_ICSR  56/57 (csr rise alone)
  M_NULL    47/57      HEAD    16/57      RESTORED 57/57, sentinel cleared on both parts

*** FINDING 1 (grok, BREACH-FOUND): THE SURVIVE-ONLY HOLE WAS STILL THERE, ON THE EIGHT
BYTES THE FIX ACTUALLY ACCEPTS. ***  The sixteen kill rows prove the host SURVIVES and the
guest runs on.  They prove NOTHING about whether the byte was stored or read back, so a
mutant that accepts the access and drops the data passes all sixteen.  **That is the same
class table 1 found at 0x1ff8** -- two consecutive findings, which is this project's
trigger to ENUMERATE THE SPACE AND CLOSE EVERY CELL IN ONE DIFF.  Nine round-trip rows
close it (0x1fef plus the eight), each writing a DISTINCT byte so that a mutant folding
offsets onto one cell is caught too.

*** FINDING 2 (grok): M_NULL AS RUN WAS NOT THE MUTANT THIS TABLE SAID IT WAS, AND THE
RECORD ABOVE WAS THEREFORE FALSE ABOUT CLAUSE (d). ***  The mutator replaced the store
with a COMMENT -- and a comment is WHITESPACE, so `goto ret;' became the if-body.  Reads
stopped taking the accept path, fell into the switch, and died at `default:'.  The leg
measured "reads are fatal everywhere", not "the store is gone": t2 shows `live absent'
rather than `live 0x0', `ok rd 1fef' exit1 against `ok wr 1fef' exit0, and **`wr 1ff0'
GREEN -- the write-side rows never saw a missing store at all.**  The block above claimed
(d) was satisfied by `live' reddening 0x5a vs 0x00; the artifact said otherwise and nobody
read it until a seat did.  Rebuilt with a real BRACED statement, and t3 now measures
exactly what was claimed: `live 0x0' plus all nine round-trips red.  **CLAUSE (d) HAS NOW
ACTUALLY BEEN RUN.**

*** FINDING 3 (deepseek, BREACH-FOUND): REFUTED, and recorded because a refutation with
its warrant is a result. ***  It proposed that widening the upper bound by one sends
0x1ff9 to `default:' with no row to see it, saying "no row tests 0x1ff9".  **The probe has
`ok rd 1ff9' and `ok wr 1ff9'** -- both would redden, because that offset would then end
the host.  The escape does not exist.

WHAT THE PANEL RATIFIED: the FIX itself, unanimously.  glm, minimax and the kimi substitute
all RATIFY; grok and deepseek both say the fix is right and aim their BREACH verdicts at
the instrument.  **No seat disputed the boundary, the arithmetic or the disposition.**
Both breach findings were about the DETECTOR and one about this table's own apparatus.
